{"seconds": 123.9, "exit": 0, "final": "After Bxc3, Black plays dxc3 or Bxf5. This trades pieces but doesn't seem as forcing as f4+.\n\nLet me also double-check that f4+ is indeed check:\n\nThe position has White pawn on f2 and Black king on e5. If the pawn moves to f4, it would attack e5. Yes, that's check.\n\nSo the key move is **f4+**, a check that forces the Black king to move, and then White has a devastating continuation with Be6+ forcing the bishop sacrifice or allowing White to win material.\n\nLet me write the coaching note now:\n\n---\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nYour opponent's king on e5 was dangerously exposed. You could have delivered check with f4+, driving the king to d5 or d6. If Kd5, then Be6+ forces the king to capture your bishop or move, and after Kxe6, you continue with f5+ and g4xf5+ to recapture with tempo\u2014winning material overall. This teaches you to look for forcing checks that exploit an exposed king. When your opponent's pieces are exposed, especially the king, deliver checks to control the board.\n\n---\n\nThe main line is:\n1. f4+ Kd5 (if Kd6, then Bxe4 wins cleanly)\n2. Be6+ Kxe6 (if Kd6, Bxc3 wins the knight)\n3. f5+ Bxf5\n4. gxf5+ Kxf5\n\nAnd White has won the bishop and a pawn.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"f4+\", \"line\": [\"f4+\", \"Kd5\", \"Be6+\", \"Kxe6\", \"f5+\", \"Bxf5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/5p1p/p3kB1P/P2pb1P1/2n3K1/1r3P2/R3B3 w - - 5 34"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/5p1p/p3kB1P/P2pb1P1/2n3K1/1r3P2/R3B3 w - - 5 34"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/5p1p/p3kB1P/P2pb1P1/2n3K1/1r3P2/R3B3 w - - 5 34"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/5p1p/p3kB1P/P2pb1P1/2n3K1/1r3P2/R3B3 w - - 5 34", "move": "f4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/5p1p/p3kB1P/P2pbPP1/2n3K1/1r6/R3B3 b - - 0